{
 "title": "Procesamiento de texto: std.string",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "El texto tiene dos formas en Greengold: **`str`** (inmutable, una vista: `\"hello\"`) y **`string`** (una secuencia UTF-8 que puede crecer en el heap). `std.string` ofrece ayudantes que funcionan con ambos."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    text = \"  apple,pear,banana  \"",
    "    trimmed = string.str_trim(text)",
    "    print(trimmed)",
    "    print(string.str_contains(trimmed, \"pear\"))",
    "    print(string.str_starts_with(trimmed, \"apple\"))",
    "    parts = string.str_split(trimmed, ',')",
    "    print(parts.len)",
    "    for p in parts:",
    "        print(p)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "apple,pear,banana",
    "true",
    "true",
    "3",
    "apple",
    "pear",
    "banana"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Para construir un `string` que pueda crecer usa `string.from`, `append_str` y `append_byte`; para imprimirlo tomas la vista de solo lectura con `as_str()`. Las conversiones a número devuelven `Optional`: `parse_i64`, `parse_f64`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    msg = string.from(\"Greengold\")",
    "    msg.append_str(\" Language\")",
    "    msg.append_byte('!')",
    "    print(msg.as_str())",
    "    print(string.parse_i64(\"42\").value_or(0))",
    "    print(string.parse_i64(\"4x2\").value_or(-1))",
    "    print(string.to_upper(\"hello\").as_str())"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Greengold Language!",
    "42",
    "-1",
    "HELLO"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c10-l02-x1",
   "prompt": "Divide el texto `\"1,2,3,4\"` por las comas, convierte cada parte con `parse_i64` e imprime su total.",
   "starter": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    total: i64 = 0",
    "    print(total)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    total: i64 = 0",
    "    parts = string.str_split(\"1,2,3,4\", ',')",
    "    for p in parts:",
    "        total += string.parse_i64(p).value_or(0)",
    "    print(total)"
   ],
   "hint": "Divide con `str_split` y suma `parse_i64(p).value_or(0)` en un bucle.",
   "expected": [
    "10"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c10-l02-q1",
   "q": "¿Qué devuelve `string.parse_i64(\"abc\")`?",
   "options": [
    "0",
    "`None` (un `Optional`)",
    "El programa se cae"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "El texto que no se puede convertir da `None`; el fallo se expresa como un valor."
  }
 ]
}
